{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>בבטן</b> — The one who explains בבטן as 'the Name decreed the matter of birthright and blessing' — I do not know what בבטן has to do with it, and Scripture says: בטרם אצרך בבטן ידעתיך (Before I formed you in the womb I knew you). And in my opinion: it is as its literal meaning, for בבטן עקב את אחיו (in the womb he supplanted his brother), and this is explicit: וידו אוחזת בעקב עשו (and his hand was grasping Esau's heel). And the meaning is: why do they not remember the children of Jacob, whose father I chose and to whom I gave supremacy over all who were born? For when he was בבטן (in the womb) I gave him strength to grasp the heel, and this is like a miraculous act, for there is no power in one standing in the placenta and at the time of its rupture to grasp anything, until he exits the womb into the air of the world — and behold, while he was בבטן I gave him his strength, and afterward he wrestled with the angel and could not overcome him, and behold, one angel killed the entire camp of Assyria, and at his appearance people are terrified — like David, who was panic-stricken, how much more so to wrestle with him. And behold, the meaning is that all the children of the world shall know that his seed will stand forever, and in the end he will defeat his enemies. And behold, Ephraim thinks that Ephraim himself found power."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "Resolved the paraphrased explanation of an unnamed commentator; the identity is not specified by Ibn Ezra and none is inferable from context."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:03.999750325Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}